! Original Dolch palettes: Renzhi Li (Belleve Invis). https://github.com/be5invis/vscode-theme-dolch
! Tide retains upstream Blue primitives; Ember uses original Alter custom ramps with the shared Blue base. Dusk, Viridian, Bloom and the application mappings are Solai studies.

! Solai Tide Dark — xterm resources; does not affect other X applications.
XTerm*background: #101416
XTerm*foreground: #C7CBCE
XTerm*cursorColor: #7BF2FF
XTerm*highlightColor: #0B4450
XTerm*highlightTextColor: #C7CBCE
XTerm*highlightColorMode: true
XTerm*color0: #101416
XTerm*color1: #EC7D71
XTerm*color2: #4DB073
XTerm*color3: #B49C43
XTerm*color4: #52A1F4
XTerm*color5: #D580C7
XTerm*color6: #00B2CA
XTerm*color7: #B0B4B7
XTerm*color8: #6F7375
XTerm*color9: #FFA798
XTerm*color10: #72E19A
XTerm*color11: #E6C964
XTerm*color12: #7CCFFF
XTerm*color13: #FFAAFB
XTerm*color14: #00E3FE
XTerm*color15: #DFE3E6
